WEBVTT

00:00:19.949 --> 00:00:21.949
What are we doing here?

00:00:21.949 --> 00:00:23.949
Well, I don't know, exactly.

00:00:23.949 --> 00:00:24.949
I got this hot tip.

00:00:24.949 --> 00:00:26.949
There's something weird going on up here.

00:00:26.949 --> 00:00:27.949
I thought it might be a good story.

00:00:27.949 --> 00:00:31.949
By weird, you mean two people at Makeout Point not making out?

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:34.359
You're right.

00:00:34.359 --> 00:00:35.359
You know what, we're undercover.

00:00:35.359 --> 00:00:37.359
We should probably be a little more convincing.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:55.409
Are you putting the move on me?

00:00:55.409 --> 00:00:57.409
No, come on.

00:00:57.409 --> 00:01:03.060
You want me to?

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.060
Okay, look.

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:09.060
I know we planted our flag on the summit of intimate territory back when we were interns, but...

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:11.060
I thought it was, and it wasn't...

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:12.060
No, it definitely was.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.060
Okay, me too. Really. I mean...

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:15.060
Really, definitely.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:20.060
And it's not like I wouldn't mind exploring that territory again, one day.

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:24.060
But I just thought maybe this time we could take it a little slower.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:31.019
Well, I'm slow.

00:01:31.019 --> 00:01:32.019
Slow is great.

00:01:32.019 --> 00:01:35.489
You can barely see me move.

00:01:35.489 --> 00:02:12.189
What was that?

00:02:12.189 --> 00:02:13.189
That came to me.

00:02:13.189 --> 00:02:14.189
from the path.

00:02:14.189 --> 00:02:15.189
Come on.

00:02:15.189 --> 00:02:16.189
Oh, yeah.

00:02:16.189 --> 00:02:18.189
We should definitely go check that out in the really dark woods.

00:02:18.189 --> 00:02:19.189
It's cool.

00:02:19.189 --> 00:02:24.300
Why would anyone want to wander around the woods?

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.300
You're probably hit for the lake.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.300
This is a really bad idea.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.300
You know, maybe we should call someone.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.090
Hello!

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:36.090
No, I was thinking more like authority figures

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.090
who can carry weapon, man?

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:59.699
Looks like the naked trail ends here.

00:02:59.699 --> 00:04:13.729
Is that?

00:04:13.729 --> 00:04:14.729
Is that the invitation for the ball?

00:04:14.729 --> 00:04:15.729
Mm-hmm.

00:04:15.729 --> 00:04:16.730
I just RSVPed.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.730
I hope Lex gets a good turnout.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.730
I can't imagine anyone from Metropolis

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:24.730
who's who list, not showing up to help the family's affected by Dark Thursday.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:29.009
You know, I, uh, I responded for two.

00:04:29.009 --> 00:04:33.319
Thanks, Mom, but costumes really aren't my thing.

00:04:33.319 --> 00:04:36.319
Besides, it's not really the place for reunion, you know?

00:04:36.319 --> 00:04:41.910
How do you feel about the two of them together?

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:50.019
Like they're different people?

00:04:50.019 --> 00:04:52.019
We all have our own ways of moving on.

00:04:52.019 --> 00:04:57.019
Whether it's about growing up or just surviving.

00:04:57.019 --> 00:05:04.189
Um, I've lost Lana, dad, Jarrell.

00:05:04.189 --> 00:05:05.189
You don't see me.

00:05:05.189 --> 00:05:06.189
It's a different person.

00:05:06.189 --> 00:05:09.189
Well, in a lot of ways I do, Clark.

00:05:09.189 --> 00:05:12.189
All those things have shaped the person you are now,

00:05:12.189 --> 00:05:25.779
and that person you'll become.

00:05:25.779 --> 00:05:27.779
I already know what the device is in Dr. Grohl.

00:05:27.779 --> 00:05:29.779
Your job is to tell me what it is.

00:05:29.779 --> 00:05:31.779
I want to report.

00:05:31.779 --> 00:05:37.420
What's all this?

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:41.420
My God, your complexion is even more radiant than in the magazines.

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:43.420
This is Monica.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:46.420
She's helping us pick out the costumes for the charity ball.

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:49.420
She can help you put something together.

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:50.420
Um, well, thank you.

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:51.420
for coming.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:52.420
But I think I can dress myself.

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:54.420
Oh, come on, Lana.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.420
I thought you'd have fun becoming anyone you wanted.

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:59.420
Well, I can tell you what I'm not.

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:01.420
The next Lex girl?

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:07.139
Monica, will you excuse us?

00:06:07.139 --> 00:06:11.920
He saw this morning's paper.

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:16.329
Look, Lana, I was raised in front of the cameras.

00:06:16.329 --> 00:06:18.329
I know it can be hurtful.

00:06:18.329 --> 00:06:23.329
When I was 13, a reporter caught me between classes at boarding school.

00:06:23.329 --> 00:06:25.329
He asked me how I felt about my mother's death.

00:06:25.329 --> 00:06:31.350
A mic shoved in my face in front of classmates I

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:44.699
couldn't stand. That's how I found out she died. The press will tear us apart if we let them.

00:06:44.699 --> 00:06:51.139
Well, they're right about the revolving door of women you've had.

00:06:51.139 --> 00:06:56.139
Maybe. But I've never asked anything to move in with me.

00:06:56.139 --> 00:07:06.209
Lex, I know you. You desire what you can't have. So what happens when you get it?

00:07:06.209 --> 00:07:11.209
I'd be lying if I said I didn't struggle against my nature every day to let myself have this with you.

00:07:11.209 --> 00:07:12.209
And I'm fighting mine to believe you.

00:07:12.209 --> 00:07:15.800
I don't believe you.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:16.800
I'm giving you time.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:19.800
I've given you space, but you still don't know what you want.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:20.800
And you do?

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:22.800
I want us to stop pretending we're only roommates.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:27.839
Lex, I just need to be sure.

00:07:27.839 --> 00:07:29.839
I always trust people too much.

00:07:29.839 --> 00:07:31.839
No, you trusted Clark too much.

00:07:31.839 --> 00:07:36.860
Now you can always come up with excuses why this won't work,

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:38.860
but you have to decide.

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:41.860
You can either fight with Clark's ghost or you can be with me.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:47.290
I'm done paying for his mistakes.

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:59.069
Hey.

00:07:59.069 --> 00:08:01.069
Hey, how goes life living with Lois?

00:08:01.069 --> 00:08:02.069
Closer to coffee, further from Santa.

00:08:02.069 --> 00:08:08.310
be further from sanity, but you know, until Metropolis University reopens, I guess what does it they say about a gift horse?

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:11.310
Stay away from the mouth, which is difficult because Lois uses her so much.

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:12.310
Right.

00:08:12.310 --> 00:08:13.310
So what's going on?

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:19.069
Okay, so I found a body in the woods up at Lone Pine last night.

00:08:19.069 --> 00:08:23.829
Girl and Guy decide to make like the birds and the bees, girl gets her wings cut, Guy buzzes off.

00:08:23.829 --> 00:08:25.829
You think he killed her?

00:08:25.829 --> 00:08:30.310
I seriously doubt some freshly minted pimple popper is physically capable of doing that.

00:08:30.310 --> 00:08:32.049
I mean, the M.O. wasn't exactly exactly...

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:35.070
normal, if you know what I mean.

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:39.059
What do you mean?

00:08:39.059 --> 00:08:44.059
Impaling people in trees in under five minutes isn't humanly possible.

00:08:44.059 --> 00:08:47.059
Unless the guy was infected with kryptonite.

00:08:47.059 --> 00:08:49.059
And that's our only lead and he's still missing.

00:08:49.059 --> 00:08:54.509
What were you doing to make out point?

00:08:54.509 --> 00:09:00.789
What's up, CK?

00:09:00.789 --> 00:09:34.179
Hey.

00:09:34.179 --> 00:09:35.179
Hey.

00:09:35.179 --> 00:09:36.179
Hi.

00:09:36.179 --> 00:09:40.059
Queen Industries.

00:09:40.059 --> 00:09:42.059
Must have caught a strong headwind.

00:09:42.059 --> 00:09:44.059
Mrs. Kent's been waiting for this for weeks. Thanks.

00:09:44.059 --> 00:09:47.559
You're welcome.

00:09:47.559 --> 00:09:55.289
Crap, I'm sorry.

00:09:55.289 --> 00:09:59.850
Just so you know, with a face like that,

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:02.850
you can do a whole lot better than playing errand boy to the rich and arrogant.

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:03.850
Here.

00:10:03.850 --> 00:10:05.850
Thank you very much. What is, uh...

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:06.850
Your tip?

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:07.850
It's a tip.

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:09.850
Okay.

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:12.850
Seriously. Aim higher.

00:10:12.850 --> 00:10:19.070
Listen, um...

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:20.070
I thought I heard the door.

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:24.070
Yeah, your pledge finally sailed in from Queen Industries.

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:26.070
Where's the man who came with it?

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:27.070
The courier?

00:10:27.070 --> 00:10:30.070
Oh, I gave him his tip and sent him on his merry little little.

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:36.379
Way.

00:10:36.379 --> 00:10:40.379
Handsome, chiseled features with a smile that could light up a barn.

00:10:40.379 --> 00:10:42.379
Mrs. Kent?

00:10:42.379 --> 00:10:44.379
You have a crush on the courier?

00:10:44.379 --> 00:10:51.379
You mean the billionaire CEO who stopped by to talk about his financial support of my platform?

00:10:51.379 --> 00:10:54.379
No, Lois, I don't. I've never even met him.

00:10:54.379 --> 00:10:56.379
And now I probably never will.

00:10:56.379 --> 00:11:02.190
That was Oliver Queen.

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:11.409
Sorry, they'd already organized a search party.

00:11:11.409 --> 00:11:13.409
And the police dogs from Granville will be here in another hour.

00:11:13.409 --> 00:11:14.909
we'll be here in another hour.

00:11:14.909 --> 00:11:16.409
Chloe, where exactly did you find the bottom?

00:11:16.409 --> 00:11:18.409
It was just up the road about a quarter mile.

00:11:18.409 --> 00:11:19.409
Okay.

00:11:19.409 --> 00:11:29.250
Guess I'll meet you there.

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:31.250
You're not supposed to be here.

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:33.250
I'm sorry?

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:38.259
I'm... I'm with the search party.

00:11:38.259 --> 00:11:40.259
Clark Kent.

00:11:40.259 --> 00:11:45.250
Gloria, Park Services.

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:48.250
They, uh, find anything yet?

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:52.870
No, nothing.

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:54.870
Have you?

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:58.120
It's a big forest.

00:11:58.120 --> 00:12:00.120
Lots of green.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:07.669
You must feel isolated out here, working all alone.

00:12:07.669 --> 00:12:11.019
There's no one for miles.

00:12:11.019 --> 00:12:12.019
No. It's...

00:12:12.019 --> 00:12:14.019
What I love about it.

00:12:14.019 --> 00:12:23.440
We haven't met before, have we?

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:33.980
I think I'd remember.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:36.980
So you, you search this whole area all by yourself?

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:38.980
A couple of times.

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:40.980
I haven't found anything that's not supposed to be here.

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:42.980
One more search wouldn't hurt.

00:12:42.980 --> 00:12:53.429
I found him. Go get help.

00:12:53.429 --> 00:12:59.100
Where are you?

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:04.299
Over here! He's alive!

00:13:04.299 --> 00:13:06.299
Oh!

00:13:06.299 --> 00:13:12.740
You're bleeding.

00:13:12.740 --> 00:13:33.840
We don't have much time.

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:35.840
Mom's in the cafeteria.

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:39.840
Wow, this guy's pretty messed up.

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:41.840
Not as bad as his girlfriend in the tree.

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:49.830
Hey, what are these things on his lungs?

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:51.830
It beats me.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:52.830
Jimmy!

00:13:52.830 --> 00:14:00.149
What? We have to get this in the paper. We have to warn people.

00:14:00.149 --> 00:14:02.149
We don't even know what it is yet.

00:14:02.149 --> 00:14:05.149
She's right. A picture of some weird x-ray isn't exactly page one material.

00:14:05.149 --> 00:14:08.149
Yeah, well, maybe we'd have a better picture if I was with you guys when you found him.

00:14:08.149 --> 00:14:10.909
Okay.

00:14:10.909 --> 00:14:14.909
Okay, that was my call. You're just so much more at home in the streets of Metropolis.

00:14:14.909 --> 00:14:16.909
I know the woods freak you out.

00:14:16.909 --> 00:14:18.909
No, no, you know what freaks me out?

00:14:18.909 --> 00:14:21.909
Is my girl traipsing through a forest when something like that can happen?

00:14:21.909 --> 00:14:23.909
Your girl?

00:14:23.909 --> 00:14:26.350
I mean, aren't you?

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:33.610
Guys, this really isn't the time.

00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:44.059
Yeah, you're right, CK. I gotta go take care or something, so we'll talk later when we're alone.

00:14:44.059 --> 00:14:52.330
So you always have fired up?

00:14:52.330 --> 00:14:55.330
You should see him when he's on his 10th cup of house trip.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:15:01.899
Are your hands?

00:15:01.899 --> 00:15:02.899
Healed.

00:15:02.899 --> 00:15:06.899
Which begs the obvious question, since not even Obi-Wan's lightsaber can gins you.

00:15:06.899 --> 00:15:09.899
You're superdamous. How did a little vine cut through it?

00:15:09.899 --> 00:15:11.899
No, no, no. But I didn't get weak, so it's not kryptonite.

00:15:11.899 --> 00:15:15.899
Well, I sent a cutting of the fine to my botany professor and let you.

00:15:15.899 --> 00:15:18.899
If it's not me or rock, what else could it be?

00:15:18.899 --> 00:15:22.899
You know, Long Pine Ridge goes right against the Luther State.

00:15:22.899 --> 00:15:26.899
There's a greenhouse that runs right near the property line. That'd be a good place to start.

00:15:26.899 --> 00:15:28.899
Okay, call me the advocate of the district.

00:15:28.899 --> 00:15:33.899
Tell me the advocate of the devil, Clark, but don't you think that pointing the pitchfork at Lex is a little bit of a stretch?

00:15:33.899 --> 00:15:35.899
He had his hands on the Kryptonian ship.

00:15:35.899 --> 00:15:37.899
He was possessed by Zod.

00:15:37.899 --> 00:15:40.899
He nearly destroyed this planet if the horns fit.

00:15:40.899 --> 00:15:44.899
Okay, fine. I'm just saying you might want to check your personals at the door.

00:15:44.899 --> 00:16:19.220
You've always had an eye for beauty.

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:30.549
It's Latin name, Formasidus falsus.

00:16:30.549 --> 00:16:34.409
Beauty that belies of dark nature.

00:16:34.409 --> 00:16:37.409
So even your plants have hidden agendas.

00:16:37.409 --> 00:16:43.570
Well, I guess it all comes down to survival of the fetus.

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:46.570
survival of the fittest, doesn't it?

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:52.389
A strange vine has cropped up over the ridge at Lone Pine.

00:16:52.389 --> 00:16:53.389
It's attacking people.

00:16:53.389 --> 00:16:56.389
And naturally, you came to my little shop of horrors

00:16:56.389 --> 00:17:01.389
to foil my ingenious plot to repopulate the planet with vegetation.

00:17:01.389 --> 00:17:08.009
Sorry, Clark, I'm all out of evil.

00:17:08.009 --> 00:17:11.009
Lana must be a calming influence on me.

00:17:11.009 --> 00:17:14.009
She's never going to fit in your world, Lex.

00:17:14.009 --> 00:17:18.009
Unlike you, I'm willing to do whatever it takes so she does.

00:17:18.009 --> 00:17:19.009
You can do.

00:17:19.009 --> 00:17:21.009
You can keep fooling yourself that you've changed,

00:17:21.009 --> 00:17:23.009
but the closer you get to Lana,

00:17:23.009 --> 00:17:27.009
the closer she is to finding out who you really are.

00:17:27.009 --> 00:17:30.009
The days of you showing up unannounced in my home are over.

00:17:30.009 --> 00:17:35.089
You're not welcome here.

00:17:35.089 --> 00:17:52.549
You found your way in, you can find your way out.

00:17:52.549 --> 00:17:56.019
Hi.

00:17:56.019 --> 00:17:58.019
It was such a rush to evacuate with the dorms.

00:17:58.019 --> 00:18:00.019
I guess I took a few of your things.

00:18:00.019 --> 00:18:02.019
Thanks.

00:18:02.019 --> 00:18:07.019
Oh, wow, I was really missing this, uh, half-chudy-raycer.

00:18:07.019 --> 00:18:09.970
And you're...

00:18:09.970 --> 00:18:12.970
library book, which is two weeks overdue.

00:18:12.970 --> 00:18:13.970
Why?

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:19.599
I don't know why, but I felt like I needed an excuse to come and talk with you.

00:18:19.599 --> 00:18:27.529
Excuse accepted. Let's go upstairs.

00:18:27.529 --> 00:18:38.400
It feels like a lifetime since I lived here.

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:42.400
Yeah, well, a sprawling 17th century mansion isn't a bad upgrade.

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:47.400
Well, actually it's getting kind of crowded in there.

00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:55.579
Water? Please. Lex seems to think that I'm dragging Clark's ghost around with me.

00:18:55.579 --> 00:18:56.559
And he didn't see.

00:18:56.579 --> 00:18:57.579
sign up for a threesome.

00:18:57.579 --> 00:19:03.869
Chloe, I have this terrible feeling.

00:19:03.869 --> 00:19:12.579
I feel like if I do this with Lex, I'm going to lose my identity.

00:19:12.579 --> 00:19:17.579
Well, Lana, if you don't trust him now, that dynamic's not going to change.

00:19:17.579 --> 00:19:21.579
It's just, I keep blaming my trust issues on everyone else.

00:19:21.579 --> 00:19:26.579
And the truth is, the person that I don't trust is myself.

00:19:26.579 --> 00:19:28.579
I keep...

00:19:28.579 --> 00:19:32.059
I haven't always made the right decisions.

00:19:32.059 --> 00:19:35.059
And when I realize that I have made the wrong last,

00:19:35.059 --> 00:19:40.299
I'm too far gone to get myself out.

00:19:40.299 --> 00:19:43.299
Lana, I don't know if Lex is the right guy for you or not.

00:19:43.299 --> 00:19:48.299
I mean, he certainly wouldn't be my first choice, but he wouldn't even really be on my list.

00:19:48.299 --> 00:19:53.299
You can't just sit safely by the water and watch all the happy people splashing around.

00:19:53.299 --> 00:19:57.299
I mean, eventually, you have to grow some fins and just dive in.

00:19:57.299 --> 00:20:37.740
God, you scared the blink at me.

00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:39.740
I thought I was the only one that felt safe out here right now.

00:20:39.740 --> 00:20:42.740
No, no, no, no, not safe, compelled.

00:20:42.740 --> 00:20:43.740
By what?

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:44.740
A guy.

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:49.740
girl. And the photo, you know, my hope, her respect, hints.

00:20:49.740 --> 00:20:53.910
Well, you have mine.

00:20:53.910 --> 00:20:55.910
Since the girl made me drop a log.

00:20:55.910 --> 00:21:01.380
Look, is there any chance that you've seen this weird vine that's fun to people?

00:21:01.380 --> 00:21:04.380
Yeah, I think I can help you find what you're looking for.

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:10.380
Uh, well, I don't know what's, um, well, I don't know about, but, um,

00:21:10.380 --> 00:21:15.910
well, you know, I already got a girl, so...

00:21:15.910 --> 00:21:17.910
I don't want to be your girl.

00:21:17.910 --> 00:21:22.759
